        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T08:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Connection is not \"tied\" to address, that\u0027s why we have connection handle as identifier. If multiple clients request connection using different RPAs, X, Y, Z, I wouldn\u0027t mind returning same handle with different addresses to each of them.\n\nOr you have to specify in callback what type of address will we return, but it can change, i.e. if you pair device on other transport.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf2bcb43_55c7ad05",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T08:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would you need that ? HCI must return invalid connection ID because it have race condition you can\u0027t work around. But if we build layer on top of it, we can hide it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95a526cd_977ca9ed",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T18:04:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that this is an async API. So when you call `connect().await`, it will effectively \"block\" the task until the connection completes. So this is for if one task calls `connect()`, then another task cancels that connection",
      "parentUuid": "bf2bcb43_55c7ad05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96eb3015_342b2634",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T08:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not just be idempotent for cancelation ? Do you really want to handle that error in each client ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70935e87_05358c3e",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T18:04:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The client can just disregard it if they don\u0027t care. But since we have this information, I thought we might as well supply it.",
      "parentUuid": "96eb3015_342b2634",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91d73694_1ee0f1d1",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
