        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T08:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you can\u0027t make this assumption.\nSome clients might want to do background connection, and bump up connection parameters by starting direct connection when having good indication device is nearby, i.e. user tapping on it in application to speed up connection.\n\nIn such case, client shouldn\u0027t be required to cancel the connection attempt first (which would modify the accept list) to start it immediately later.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "930fae87a74712a0f638f225c78de6afd864f2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
